/*
==============================================================================
  ESP32-S3 UWB Tag Firmware for MaUWB DW3000
  UDP Streaming with Kalman Filter & Adaptive Offset Correction
==============================================================================

   Project Overview:
  - This firmware configures an ESP32-S3 as a UWB Tag using the MaUWB DW3000.
  - It receives ranging data from anchors and applies per-anchor Kalman filtering.
  - Adaptive offset correction improves short- and long-range accuracy.
  - The filtered distance data is transmitted over UDP to a remote server
    (e.g., Jetson or Raspberry Pi) for processing or visualization.
  - OLED display shows tag ID and system information for field debugging.

   Key Features:
  - UWB module configured as Tag via AT+SETCFG
  - Real-time Kalman filtering with per-anchor state
  - Adaptive offset correction based on range threshold (<2.5m = 30cm, ≥2.5m = 50cm)
  - UDP client stream to specified host and port
  - OLED-based local feedback for UWB role and connected anchors

   Hardware Configuration:
  - Microcontroller: ESP32-S3
  - UWB Module: MaUWB DW3000 via HardwareSerial2 (TXD: 17, RXD: 18)
  - Display: SSD1306 OLED via I2C (SDA: GPIO 39, SCL: GPIO 38)
  - Reset Pin: GPIO 16

   Network Configuration:
  - WiFi SSID: "EB-Akatemia25"
  - UDP Host: 192.168.1.102
  - Port: 5000

   UWB & Kalman Configuration:
  - UWB_INDEX: Tag device ID
  - UWB_TAG_COUNT: Number of anchors expected
  - Kalman Parameters (per anchor):
      - Estimate: 0.0
      - Error Covariance: 1.0
      - Process Noise: 0.01
      - Measurement Noise: 0.5

   Dependencies:
  - Wire v2.0.0
  - Adafruit GFX Library v1.11.7
  - Adafruit SSD1306 v2.5.7
  - Adafruit BusIO v1.14.4
  - SPI v2.0.0

   Author: Lenni Kiviniemi and Samu Heinonen
   Last Updated: 2025-04-15
==============================================================================
*/



